module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.stale_present_tense_coverage_claim_in_the_authority_consulted_first

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data stale_present_tense_coverage_claim_in_the_authority_consulted_first: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "stale_present_tense_coverage_claim_in_the_authority_consulted_first" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a declaration's own annotation asserts, in the present tense, that an invariant it just gave up is still covered elsewhere, and names a consumer that does not execute** (INVALID STATE: a de-enrolment, re-home or scope narrowing lands together with a sentence of the form \"enforcement is NOT reduced: it executes per-PR via X\", and X is on no executing path. ",

    "HARM: the sentence is not merely unhelpful, it is load-bearing in the wrong direction. ",

    "It sits in the authority a reader consults FIRST when asking whether a class is still covered, so it converts an open question into a confident YES, and the reader stops. ",

    "The de-enrolment that produced it was usually correct on its own terms -- a corpus walk priced out of the per-PR fold, a nullary gate that should never have been tree-grain -- which is exactly why the compensating sentence is written with no one checking it: the author is discharging a real objection and the sentence is how the objection is discharged. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. It is not an inert lens (the mechanism may be perfectly live), not a rung drop (nothing is declared), and not an ordinary stale comment (an ordinary stale comment describes; this one ASSERTS COVERAGE, which is the fact a reviewer is trying to establish). ",

    "The tell is grammatical and mechanical: a present-tense executes/runs/covers clause naming an entry or function, inside an annotation whose subject is a REMOVAL. ",

    "SPECIMEN ONE, and it is the one this class was filed from. ",

    "`v2.compiler.compile`'s annotation beside `required_compile_lens_roster` (the single registration roster that replaced the two grain-specific lists, gunbc#11004) records the de-enrolment of `lens_module_gate` from the root roster and adds that \"Enforcement is NOT reduced: the invariant executes per-PR via its honestly-stamped consumer v2.test.claim.enforcement.lens_module_gate_witness\". ",

    "That is false on two independent grounds, either sufficient alone: the entry is enrolled in `gunbc.witness_deferral_freeze`, which means DECLARED NEVER-EXECUTED, and `test/claim/enforcement/` is a pattern in `gunbc.ci_layer_roots` `witness_exclusion_frontier`, which carves the whole directory out of per-PR discovery. ",

    "SPECIMEN TWO, prior and already corrected, which is what establishes this as recurring rather than singular. ",

    "`gunbc.ci_layer_roots` `excl_bin_wet_reason` read \"they run every PR as the declared bin-witness wet batch via bin_witness_wet_entries\" while nothing had run that batch since the 2026-08-15 floor cut -- 94 rows across 38 entry files naming an executing consumer that did not execute. ",

    "It was corrected in place on 2026-08-19 with the correction stated rather than the sentence quietly reworded, and that correction's own note gives this class its severity in one line: anyone reading the row to answer \"is this class covered\" was told YES. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. ",

    "The only thing standing between the false sentence and a reader is review diligence, and both specimens survived review at the time they landed. ",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable, and the reason it is not higher is that the sentence is prose in an annotation, which by DESIGN section 4c no Accepted program can read. ",

    "The class cannot climb by making the annotation checkable; it climbs by making the CLAIM a declaration. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER: a de-enrolment carries a typed compensating-consumer row -- the removed obligation, the entry and function said to still cover it -- so the claim joins `gunbc.witness_deferral_freeze` and `gunbc.ci_layer_roots` `witness_exclusion_frontier` the way `gunbc.v2_compile_obligation_census` now derives every obligation's per-PR standing, and a compensating consumer that executes nowhere refuses at the point the de-enrolment lands rather than being discovered by a census months later.)"
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.compile", decl_name: "required_compile_lens_roster"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "excl_bin_wet_reason"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "witness_exclusion_frontier"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.witness_deferral_freeze", decl_name: "frozen_path_deferrals"),
    decl_ref(
      module_path: "gunbc.v2_compile_obligation_census",
      decl_name: "interpreted_standing"
    ),
  ],
}
